  After renewing my interest in NetHack with v3.1.3, I have thought
of a new tool that might be useful. I hate accidently setting off traps
that are in front of doors or in corriders.

Tool: a board ( or: a piece of wood)
Application: Used to 'disarm' traps. When you 'a' with direction, you
	can cover a trapdoor, block arrow/dart traps, etc.
Obtained: ^D doors, killing wood golems, hardware stores

There could be different 'types' plywood, balsa, pine, oak.

If a player or monster walks over a disamred trap with a board, there is
a chance that the board 'break' and sets off the trap. The possiblity depends
on the characters weight vs. the board type. ( i.e. a dragon 
walking over a piece of plywood would certainly break the wood as opposed to a
newt.)

When disarming the trap, then there is a chance of setting off the trap
depending on the characters dexerity.

If the board is cursed/blessed then the possiliblityes of setting off the
trap would be alterated.

Anyway, just some ideas.

